changelog_entry: >-
  Run-setup revision 16 (`history/v16.patch`, kind run_setup): the lead's write
  boundary becomes a guard, and the seat lifecycle is stated once. write_limits.deny
  gains two lead-bound globs - the workflow's package repository and the user's memory
  directory - each with its reason and remedy (user-owned surfaces; the
  2026-09-05 to 09-08 incident). roles.lead states the seat lifecycle: a doer retires
  only on the passing review outcome, a reviewer gets one frozen stamp after every
  constraint reached the producer, a record is read after its mtime settles; the
  scheduling restatement there and realize_increment's second copy of the
  retained-thread rule are cut. Graph meaning unchanged (21 nodes, 67 edges, 5 control
  nodes after revision 15). Three release-layer follow-ups named: the deny mode should
  match Bash write targets, not every path token; globs need a home-relative form; git
  commands that write files under a directory-only token (apply, checkout, merge,
  cherry-pick, stash pop) escape the deny.
